## Outcome and conditions

Produce a critical explanation of the chapter’s chain from political constraints to entry/property/finance incentives, comparing post-independence paths, invention and banking, and Gates/Slim. Distinguish talent from the opportunities/constraints rules create and include exclusions, dated comparisons and limits on causal identification.

Essential criterion components are **C1 political-economic incentive chain, C2 independence and finance mechanisms, C3 Gates-Slim institutional comparison, C4 exclusions and causal-evidence limits**. Primary finished-note locations: [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Colonial_Institutions_and_Divergence.md#Different paths after independence]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Colonial_Institutions_and_Divergence.md#From political rules to invention, firms, and finance]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Colonial_Institutions_and_Divergence.md#Carlos Slim, Bill Gates, and the limits of business power]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Colonial_Institutions_and_Divergence.md#What the authors mean by institutions]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Colonial_Institutions_and_Divergence.md#Answers to the six assigned reading questions]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Colonial_Institutions_and_Divergence.md#Synthesis]].

