## Prerequisites and checks

O006 supplies beneficiary/feedback logic and O007 supplies colonial comparison. O008-P1 / 1: “Why could a privileged group resist a reform that raises broad prosperity?” Key group may lose rents/control; resources/effective influence defend rules while diffuse reformers bear organizing costs. Pass requires incentive plus power/collective mechanism; partial misses one; fail assumes aggregate gain ensures reform. Repair O006 W1/S1. O008-P2 / 1: “Were the Virginia assembly/headrights universal inclusion or a relative expansion?” Key relative, voting exclusions and dispossession/slavery remain. Repair O007 if omitted. Skip each with adequate committed prerequisite acquisition.

For every P diagnostic, ask before exposing its key. Pass requires all explicitly requested distinctions and their reasons; partial means a correct part with an omission or local arithmetic slip; fail means the essential prerequisite mechanism is contradicted. Unknown help or no answer is unscorable. Diagnostics are brief route selection only and never acquisition evidence. Apply the named repair once, then instruction rather than repeat-testing.

